course: dictionary
lesson: 3664
title: A word you can picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your head. A fist is a hand with the fingers bent tightly into the palm. Read the words around it to check: «He made a fist and held it tight.» The word tight tells you the fingers are pressed hard together.
explain: A fist can also be a friendly signal. «Ella gave Sam a fist bump after the match.» The word bump and the friendly match tell you a fist bump is a tap with closed hands, not a punch.
explain: Context shows how a fist is being used and how someone feels. «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the fists clench.» Clench means squeeze tight, so here the fists show anger. Read the clues to know which meaning fits.
fact: A fist is a hand with the fingers bent tightly into the palm.
fact: To clench your fist means to squeeze it tight.
fact: A fist bump is a friendly tap with closed hands, often between friends.
fact: Anger can make the fists clench, but words are the better way to sort out problems.
fact: A fist grip holds a pencil badly and tires the hand fast; a tripod grip, with the pencil between thumb and first finger, is better.
exercise: «He made a fist and held it tight.» What is a fist? | A loud shout across the playground | A foot with the toes curled up | A small bag of coins | *A hand with the fingers bent tightly into the palm
exercise: «Ella gave Sam a fist bump after the match.» What is a fist bump? | A kick with the foot | A loud shout across the pitch | *A friendly tap with closed hands | A way to hold a pencil
exercise: «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the fists clench.» What does clench mean? | Lose sight of | *Squeeze tight | Throw far away | Open wide
test: «When he felt angry, he chose words, not fists, to sort out the problem.» What does the lesson say we should use to sort out problems? | Running away | Shouting | Fists | *Words
test: Which phrase means a friendly tap with closed hands? | *Fist bump | Hand over fist | Bang your fist | Clench your fist
exam: In «The tripod grip holds the pencil; a fist grip tires the hand fast», what does the word tires tell you about a fist grip? | *It makes the hand get tired quickly | It makes the pencil write faster | It makes the hand feel fresh and strong | It makes the pencil glow
